{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin","id":957507,"title":"are siberia and the formes asian soviet states populated by cainites or kueijin?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-25T04:17:28-07:00","id":957507,"title":"are siberia and the formes asian soviet states populated by cainites or kueijin?","content":"cainites does seem like the logical answer for historical reasons. but i don't recall any book talking about this<br /> <br /> (e.g kazakhstan tajikistan etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:16:30-07:00","id":957601,"title":"","content":"Well, Siberia and the Far East are still part of Russia, so they are likely Kindred territory, as the natives were killed by the genocidal practices of Tsarist Russia. The Central Asian states are still Asian and were traditionally influenced by China (they were not colonized by Russia until the 19th century), so I would make them Kuei-jin territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:34:13-07:00","id":957663,"title":"","content":"There are Dark Ages supplements that touch on Cainites in Central Asia so I would say they're at least a presence there. <br /> <br /> Siberia is sort of weird situation as it, Mongolia, and Manchuria have a lot of demographic mixing going on that doesn't fit neatly into a dichotomy of East Asian vs Not-East Asian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:35:32-07:00","id":957664,"title":"","content":"Winds from the East sort of covers this. The answer is any place the Mongols conquered towards gives a chance of KJ. There will still be Kindred there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:01:13-07:00","id":957757,"title":"","content":"Didn\u2019t Baba Yaga take over Russia and purge the former high clans or something? Or did I dream that?<br /> <br /> No, that happened, just looked it up on the White Wolf Wiki. Apparently she died in 2000. Any word on what's happened since?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:12:29-07:00","id":957798,"title":"","content":"Which suggests that Siberia and Far East Russia would be open for colonization by the Kuei-jin (the Central Asian Republics split from the USSR before Baba Yaga awakened again, so I think they were not impacted by her activities). After all, they are closer than the Kindred, though I would hate to be the ones sent up north (I doubt that the Kuei-jin enjoy the eternal sun of summer anymore than the Kindred).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:23:56-07:00","id":957807,"title":"","content":"For me, i have made it mostly Canites.. however Kuei-jin are making inroads..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:42:16-07:00","id":958843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin#post957507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cainites does seem like the logical answer for historical reasons. but i <br /> don't recall any book talking about this<br /> <br /> (e.g kazakhstan tajikistan etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>Russia and Siberia are kindred land for sure, they have always been inhabited by tzimisce, ravnos and gangrel, and later by brujah,nosferatu and ventrue.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Tajikistan and so on I think there are good chances we are speaking of assamite lands.<br /> <br /> Kue-jin are more rooted in China, Japan,southeast Asia and north-eastern India, while west of Kolkata is vampire land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-27-2016, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T13:02:37-07:00","id":958856,"title":"","content":"Short answer: Cainites.<br /> <br /> Long answer:<br /> <br /> Siberia was wilderness and not urbanized until the last few centuries. There would be very few vampires there other than wandering ones adapted to wilderness survival. It would be lupine territory. When the Russians colonized the region post 1600, the cities they built would be populated by Kindred coming from Russia.<br /> <br /> Central Asia was a long inhabited and urbanized region. Samarkand is one of the oldest inhabited cities in the world. Central Asia was part of the Persian cultural region for most of history. Its cities would populated by vampires coming from the Middle East. Chinese influence in Central Asia didn't arise until the Tang Dynasty although obviously the Silk Road trade had been occurring since 200 BC. But by either time, Cainites would be there for two thousand years or so.<br /> <br /> Chinese power and cultural influence existed north of the Great Wall, but was limited because of the barbarians. It was mostly projected east towards Korea and Japan, and south into Indochina (where obviously Indian influence was also heavy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T13:18:45-07:00","id":958865,"title":"","content":"I was thinking to myself that the Battle of Talas in 751 probably sealed the deal on Cainite influence over Central Asia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T13:23:58-07:00","id":958867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=957664#post957664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Winds from the East sort of covers this. The answer is any place the Mongols conquered towards gives a chance of KJ. There will still be Kindred there.</div> </div> </div> </div>(weren't mongols a wide assortment of Andas and Gangrels?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T21:57:24-07:00","id":959088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=958867#post958867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (weren't mongols a wide assortment of Andas and Gangrels?)</div> </div> </div> </div>And there are also a lot of Hungry Dead from the region, many of whom participated in the ritual that annhilated the Anda bloodline. For what it's worth, Mongolia is also Beast Courts territory on the Werewolf side of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T04:19:01-07:00","id":959171,"title":"","content":"allright, though i think i will give a few small parts of siberia to the kuei jin northern manchuria for instance was only annexed by russia in the mid 19 century. perhaps even the land a bit north of mongolia<br /> <br /> i know that the parts northern of iran should be cainites they were part of many persian empires. but what about kazakhstan?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T04:47:02-07:00","id":959176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959088#post959088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And there are also a lot of Hungry Dead from the region, many of whom participated in the ritual that annhilated the Anda bloodline. For what it's worth, Mongolia is also Beast Courts territory on the Werewolf side of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's this ritual? I never read blood and silk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T06:54:13-07:00","id":959213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959171#post959171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i know that the parts northern of iran should be cainites they were part of many persian empires. but what about kazakhstan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kazakhstan would be probably be majority Cainite, though it wouldn't be impossible for there to be Kue-Jin hanging around. <br /> <br /> I'm not intimately familiar with the metaphysical rules for Kue-Jin creation, what is the minimum threshold of cultural cosmology for someone to come back as a Kue-Jin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:05:50-07:00","id":959221,"title":"","content":"That you were raised in an Asian culture and went to Hell because of your sins. Kazakhstan is an Asian culture, though it is a central Asian culture whose Kindred population would have probably killed off the local Kuei-jin during Russian rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:30:12-07:00","id":959235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959221#post959221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That you were raised in an Asian culture and went to Hell because of your sins. Kazakhstan is an Asian culture, though it is a central Asian culture whose Kindred population would have probably killed off the local Kuei-jin during Russian rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kazakhstan is about seventy percent Muslim and twenty five percent Christian though, neither of which generally support a Kue-Jin cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T09:10:03-07:00","id":959294,"title":"","content":"Religion does not matter, there are Christian and Muslim Kuei-jin, it is cultural identity that seems to matter. Do you belong to an Asian culture (even a hybrid Asian culture such as that found in Singapore or the American Chinatowns)? If so, then you have a chance of becoming a Kuei-jin. I would say that the Kindred and Kuei-jin have probably been fighting since the beginning of the Kindred, though the Antediluvians and the Methusalahs probably exterminated the Southwest Asian Kuei-jin traditions during prehistoric times, and any chih-mei are probably mistakenly exterminated as wights by Southwest Asian Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T09:38:01-07:00","id":959305,"title":"","content":"Except that even long-term habitation along the West Coast of North America by enclaves that retained their Asian customs explicitly cannot produce Kuei-jin. One of the key problems of the Great Leap Outwards.... all replacement fighters had to be brought over from the Old Country while the Kindred could replace/expand their numbers much much more efficiently. And the definition of what constitutes &quot;Asian&quot; culture seems pretty loose. Indonesia is riddled with Kuei-jin, but it's the traditional, indigenous, non-Han-acculturated culture that produces the pennangalan, who are oh so quintessentially Kuei-jin as depicted in the core books of KoE.<br /> <br /> A snapshot of the larger Kuei-jin world seems to be addressed more in Blood &amp; Silk and Wind from the East than it does in the modern books. There was a sort of &quot;collapse&quot; back towards the Middle Kingdom (except where it wasn't, vide Indonesia above and, oh yeah, what's going on in India) that occurred after the end of the Age of Beautiful Sorrow and that's the region on which the modern books focus, but Kuei-jin are out there beyond the boundaries. I remember that some of this was taken up a bit in Heretics of the Way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T10:16:04-07:00","id":959319,"title":"","content":"What is the Kue-Jin definition of &quot;Asian&quot; then? It's seems incredibly nebulous and arbitrary, which makes me question why it even exists as a distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T10:23:05-07:00","id":959323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959319#post959319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Kue-Jin definition of &amp;quot;Asian&amp;quot; then? It's seems incredibly nebulous and arbitrary, which makes me question why it even exists as a distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lands over which the 10,000 Immortals shepherded, or where the descendents of those lands settle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And there supposed to be a sizeable number of Muslim and Christian Wan Kuei.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T10:55:32-07:00","id":959334,"title":"","content":"first of all asia is very big. obviously the kuei jin do not rule iran for instance.<br /> <br /> in generally is kazakhstan more culturally east as in chinese or east as in persia?<br /> <br /> i know it's a generalisation but still..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T12:12:51-07:00","id":959366,"title":"","content":"I'd have them be entirely or almost entirely dominated by western vampires. Kuei-Jin are linked to the religions and cultures of eastern Asia. China, Korea, Japan, and so on. Russia and the former Soviet States are pretty much entirely western ideologically. I include Islam as western in this particular context. <br /> <br /> I also don't really see Kuei-Jin making any inroads into Siberia. That isn't a very hospitable place for vampires of any kind, and I can't see many Chinese born and raised Kuei-Jin deliberately heading west to live in a desolate wilderness away from food sources and civilization. Kindred, on the other hand, can be embraced into the local culture. So a Siberian native who is embraced by a kindred (almost certainly a Gangrel) is more likely to remain in their homeland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T12:53:28-07:00","id":959379,"title":"","content":"Yes, North Asia is rather inhospitable, which is probably why the ancients would spend people there as punishment. And Asian communities in the Americas explicitly create Kuei-jin, they are specifically mentioned in the KotE Players Companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:15:05-07:00","id":959401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959176#post959176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's this ritual? I never read blood and silk.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not in Blood and Silk; it happened a long time after that, and I believe is tucked away as a future event in Winds From the East.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:23:38-07:00","id":959405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959379#post959379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, North Asia is rather inhospitable, which is probably why the ancients would spend people there as punishment. And Asian communities in the Americas explicitly create Kuei-jin, they are specifically mentioned in the KotE Players Companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that it's NOT possible. The Second Breath does not happen outside the somewhat vaguely defined Middle Kingdom. That's 100% explicit. It was such a problem that the Extraordinary Commission for the Reification of Borders commissioned a Giovanni sub-clan to mess with the Shroud in California specifically so that it would be possible for new Kuei-jin to arise there. Which didn't work.<br /> <br /> It seems like the regions in which Kuei-jin can return are associated with the regions of the Five August Courts of the Fourth Age, NOT the Sinocentric Quincunx of the Fifth. The Five August Courts encompassed larger areas which included regions outside of direct Chinese influence. Maybe Chinese influence-adjacent would be sorta appropriate, but, again it doesn't REALLY encompass the regions in question... India has it's own Kuei-jin that really never have had anything to do with either set of courts. The Golden Courts of Malaysia and Indonesia aren't really very Han-influenced either.<br /> <br /> Winds of the East specifically addresses the Kuei-jin and Kindred of Mongolia and gives a more than a passing mention of the situation along the Mongol's route to Europe, effectively addressing the concerns of this question directly vis-a-vis an earlier era. Since the limiting factor seems to be something along the lines of &quot;Kuei-jin arise where they have been known to do so since days of yore&quot; checking out the earlier material probably comes closest to answering the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:46:54-07:00","id":959436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959401#post959401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not in Blood and Silk; it happened a long time after that, and I believe is tucked away as a future event in Winds From the East.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think the Anda didn't get genocided, instead they just became gangrel as they embraced other cultures. Like Karsh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T14:22:14-07:00","id":959471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959405#post959405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that it's NOT possible. The Second Breath does not happen outside the somewhat vaguely defined Middle Kingdom. That's 100% explicit. It was such a problem that the Extraordinary Commission for the Reification of Borders commissioned a Giovanni sub-clan to mess with the Shroud in California specifically so that it would be possible for new Kuei-jin to arise there. Which didn't work.<br /> <br /> It seems like the regions in which Kuei-jin can return are associated with the regions of the Five August Courts of the Fourth Age, NOT the Sinocentric Quincunx of the Fifth. The Five August Courts encompassed larger areas which included regions outside of direct Chinese influence. Maybe Chinese influence-adjacent would be sorta appropriate, but, again it doesn't REALLY encompass the regions in question... India has it's own Kuei-jin that really never have had anything to do with either set of courts. The Golden Courts of Malaysia and Indonesia aren't really very Han-influenced either.<br /> <br /> Winds of the East specifically addresses the Kuei-jin and Kindred of Mongolia and gives a more than a passing mention of the situation along the Mongol's route to Europe, effectively addressing the concerns of this question directly vis-a-vis an earlier era. Since the limiting factor seems to be something along the lines of &quot;Kuei-jin arise where they have been known to do so since days of yore&quot; checking out the earlier material probably comes closest to answering the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kanbujian - the only Mandarin word in KotE to be given with tone markers! And also the term for Hungry Dead who rise outside of the borders of what was assumed to be Hungry Dead territory. See also page 129 of the KotE Companion. I think there may also be more about them in SF By Night, but don't have the book.<br /> <br /> (Also, you're leaving out South Asia as a place where the Hungry Dead happen.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T14:27:07-07:00","id":959475,"title":"","content":"I agree. Kuei-jin can arise outside of the Middle Kingdom. The Kanbujian (Kindred of the East Companion, p. 128-129) are Kuei-jin who arise in the West.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T07:33:07-07:00","id":959803,"title":"","content":"how does one define/chinese/japanese/etc culture. especially if we take religion and philosophy(e.g legalism confucianism) out of the equation.<br /> for instance let's say someone thinks of himself as a chinese american.<br /> <br /> basically what are the core characteristis of east asian culture as opposed to western or other cultures.<br /> <br /> and finally does one need to also be east asian &quot;biologically&quot;? that is can we have a subsaharan african kueijin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T09:24:55-07:00","id":959861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959471#post959471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kanbujian - the only Mandarin word in KotE to be given with tone markers! And also the term for Hungry Dead who rise outside of the borders of what was assumed to be Hungry Dead territory. See also page 129 of the KotE Companion. I think there may also be more about them in SF By Night, but don't have the book.<br /> <br /> (Also, you're leaving out South Asia as a place where the Hungry Dead happen.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Once you mention Indonesia, Malaysia and have referenced Singapore, along with India, it gets pedantic to mention every nation involved. Open questions remain about, say, New Guinea, Melanisian islands, the rest of Polynesia, what the hell is going on in Australia (much less New Zealand) and I can't remember what has been specifically said about the Philllipines (though they seem like they would get lumped in with the Scarlet Courts?). <br /> <br /> Almost everything that deals with the Great Leap Outwards goes into how the Second Breath NEVER happens in America. At length. It's a major plot point. Check out the White Wolf Wikia if you don't want to wade through all the books. As to whether there is a contradiction in what White Wolf says. Well that NEVER happened (dripping sarcasm), but, with my lawyer hat on, I'd go with the later stuff over the former. In places other than America, I would probably go with &quot;ancestral extent&quot; to determine if it was possible, plus, probably, the beliefs of the decedent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T09:28:48-07:00","id":959864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959436#post959436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think the Anda didn't get genocided, instead they just became gangrel as they embraced other cultures. Like Karsh.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The Northern one of the August Courts were not big fans and figured out how to use their superior mojo to off the Anda. They were heavily Yin-aspected, so it's not far-fetched they had a lot of relevant power to throw out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T09:30:54-07:00","id":959865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959803#post959803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how does one define/chinese/japanese/etc culture. especially if we take religion and philosophy(e.g legalism confucianism) out of the equation.<br /> for instance let's say someone thinks of himself as a chinese american.<br /> <br /> basically what are the core characteristis of east asian culture as opposed to western or other cultures.<br /> <br /> and finally does one need to also be east asian &quot;biologically&quot;? that is can we have a subsaharan african kueijin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vide was Eldagusto said above. <br /> <br /> It doesn't have as much to do with biology or culture as it does with if the area was under the guardianship of the 10,000 Immortals before they crapped all over everything and got themselves demoted to hellspawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T09:34:40-07:00","id":959866,"title":"","content":"I think that the defining characteristic of becoming Kuei-jin is that it is linked with Asian cultures (not necessarily East Asia cultures) and has nothing to do with Confucian values, since Kuei-jin predate Confucius by thousands of years (the Kuei-jin of China would disagree because they see themselves as the center of Kuei-jin culture and keep to Confucian values). I would think that a non-Asian that adopted Asian cultural values could become Kuei-jin, regardless of their location of birth or death, while an Asian that rejected Asian cultural values would not become Kuei-jin, regardless of their location of birth or death. As for the Second Breath never happening in America, look at the KotE Companion, pp. 128-129, for what happens when Kuei-jin do take the Second Breath in America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T11:36:03-07:00","id":959923,"title":"","content":"What defines &quot;Asian&quot; culture then? Especially over thousands of years of shifting demographics and beliefs? If it doesn't have anything to do with a specific religious belief in the Kue-Jin's set dressing (which itself also doesn't make much sense) then where is the cut off? Just saying &quot;Asian&quot; is both arbitrary and unhelpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T01:08:47-07:00","id":962155,"title":"","content":"Indeed it is. There is no good official answer - if you want Kuei-Jin in your setting I recommend sitting down and working the related metaphysics out for yourself. Personally I think the whole thing is a hornet's nest so I just don't use 'em - go to China or Japan in my WoD and you will find Kindred, same as everywhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T09:39:53-07:00","id":962337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959861#post959861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Almost everything that deals with the Great Leap Outwards goes into how the Second Breath NEVER happens in America. At length. It's a major plot point. Check out the White Wolf Wikia if you don't want to wade through all the books. As to whether there is a contradiction in what White Wolf says. Well that NEVER happened (dripping sarcasm), but, with my lawyer hat on, I'd go with the later stuff over the former. In places other than America, I would probably go with &quot;ancestral extent&quot; to determine if it was possible, plus, probably, the beliefs of the decedent.</div> </div> </div> </div>San Francisco by Night has some speculation on this that the fact that Kanbujian appear is a sign of the impending Sixth Age, if I remember correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3568-philhor","name":"PhilHor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T09:25:28-07:00","id":963734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin#post957507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cainites does seem like the logical answer for historical reasons. but i don't recall any book talking about this<br /> <br /> (e.g kazakhstan tajikistan etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>Cainites are everywere, and with the russian egemony in the soviet, could have their way more often than not.<br /> Then, if the whole Baba Yaga thing is still canon, she has probably &quot;cleaned up&quot; the area from &quot;indipendent forces&quot; like the local kuei-jin (ehi... this could make and interesting chronicle... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think the limits of the Kuei-jin are the traditional areas of the classic &quot;asian&quot; philosophies (a not unfolded stack of Buddhism, Hinduism, Chinese, Japanese and south-estern tribal traditions). As reference I think you can use this image<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://image.slidesharecdn.com/3-4asianreligions-120904221230-phpapp02/95/asian-religions-3-728.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://image.slidesharecdn.com/3-4asianreligions-120904221230-phpapp02/95/asian-religions-3-728.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://image.slidesharecdn.com/3-4asianreligions-120904221230-phpapp02/95/asian-religions-3-728.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://image.slidesharecdn.com/3-4asianreligions-120904221230-phpapp02/95/asian-religions-3-728.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> for the asian sovietic areas where the tribal religions are still observed, i think the only ones that can generate Kuei-jin (Kanbujian) are the ones with a distinct east-asian ethnicity (mind you, I'm only oversimplifying)<br /> <a href=\"https://s3.postimg.io/9h88dpq2r/Ethnic_Families.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://s3.postimg.io/9h88dpq2r/Ethnic_Families.jpg</a><br /> so, not the russian animistic Uralic areas, but more often the animistic Turkic and Tungusic, maybe even the Paleo Siberian areas.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T16:22:13-07:00","id":963963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959803#post959803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how does one define/chinese/japanese/etc culture. especially if we take religion and philosophy(e.g legalism confucianism) out of the equation.<br /> for instance let's say someone thinks of himself as a chinese american.<br /> <br /> basically what are the core characteristis of east asian culture as opposed to western or other cultures.<br /> <br /> and finally does one need to also be east asian &quot;biologically&quot;? that is can we have a subsaharan african kueijin?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the African was culturally Chinese or Korean or Japanese or Indian, then perhaps. ST fiat, etc, etc. What makes it Asian? If it looks like anime, apparently... But I jest. The truth is that it's not an easy judgement to make.<br /> <br /> The subcontinent is considered KJ territory in KotE, but prior to that, it had a developed Kindred population in canon. I'd say the subcontinent is more of a mix than the other places and so, for a quick and dirty guide to what counts as 'Eastern enough', can be considered the divider between Kuei-jin and Kindred territory. East of India, it's KJ land; West is Kindred land. In the middle is a bit of both. North is Baba Yaga's territory (lupines with a few scattered Kindred). South is ocean. That's probably the simplest way to organise it in your head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 09-05-2016, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T02:15:12-07:00","id":966115,"title":"","content":"In the Dark Ages Gangrel novel there was a part where Qarakh and Aajav met a Kue-Jin. That was on the mongolian steppe and the author paints it as a very rare thing. For me who isn't familiar with KotE, this was such a cool read, how the author really makes this demon-thingy exotic and alien.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/629-anda","name":"anda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T04:06:47-07:00","id":966141,"title":"","content":"Considering the low population densities of the Mongolian steppe during the Dark Ages (4 people per square mile seems to be a good estimate), meeting a Kuei-jin would have to be a rare event because they cannot feed off of animals. That one Kuei-jin would probably have a territory of 2,500 to 25,000 square miles, so the probability of randomly meeting him would have probably been 1:2,500 at best, and that would have only been if you were not avoiding human populations. If you were, I doubt your probability would have been better than 1:1,000,000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T18:33:09-07:00","id":966515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=966141#post966141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the low population densities of the Mongolian steppe during the Dark Ages (4 people per square mile seems to be a good estimate), meeting a Kuei-jin would have to be a rare event because they cannot feed off of animals. That one Kuei-jin would probably have a territory of 2,500 to 25,000 square miles, so the probability of randomly meeting him would have probably been 1:2,500 at best, and that would have only been if you were not avoiding human populations. If you were, I doubt your probability would have been better than 1:1,000,000.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but if you join the Golden horde you can stock up on murder blood. Sooo... being nomads... That being Said Mongolian Wan Kuei are mentioned and have settled outside Mongolia. Also I can imagine Ancestors Returning to the Steppes, when they learn to feed off the Land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:28:12-07:00","id":966630,"title":"","content":"Or just off of the nomads. Either way, they would not tolerate Kindred in their territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:07:04-07:00","id":966805,"title":"","content":"Except of course, they did. Or, at least, it took a long time for them to get peeved enough to take significant (nigh-apocalyptic) action and wiped out regional Gangrel and Salubri variants. Vide <i>Wind from the East </i>(where this particularly sub-issue is front and center) and <i>Blood and Silk </i>(where it's tangential but on point).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:54:37-07:00","id":967024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=966805#post966805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except of course, they did. Or, at least, it took a long time for them to get peeved enough to take significant (nigh-apocalyptic) action and wiped out regional Gangrel and Salubri variants. Vide <i>Wind from the East </i>(where this particularly sub-issue is front and center) and <i>Blood and Silk </i>(where it's tangential but on point).</div> </div> </div> </div>The ritual required rolling Dobrul and making his torpid form into a beacon, so they might not have had a proper opportunity prior to the bloodline founder waking up hungry and dumb in later times and being a ready target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T00:02:20-07:00","id":967209,"title":"","content":"Its worth pointing out that just because the kuei-jin aren't native to a region, that doesn't mean they can't visit or move there. The Great Leap Outwards is an excellent example - the first phase involves an invasion of California, but some planners are already looking beyond, to possible attacks on South America and Australia.<br /> <br /> Less drastic examples are common, too. Looking just at the Crane dharma - one of their bodhisattvas (Rise Majestically to Greet the Sun, I think) went on a global pilgrimage, successfully circumnavigating the globe . . . oh, a good millennium before Magellan. There's also a heretical faction (&quot;Fellowship of the Travelers of the Great Earth&quot;) that believes the kuei-jin messiah will be born in &quot;barbarian lands&quot;. Adherents adopt the name (Number) Seeker in the (Direction), and explore in that direction, seeking the prophesized savior. So its perfectly appropriate for someone in Siberia to run into Third Seeker in the North, or for an Australian to meet the Eighth Seeker in the South.<br /> <br /> Kuei-jin have even visited (modern day) Europe, stronghold of the Camarilla . . .although that didn't exactly go well for them. . .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/957507-are-siberia-and-the-formes-asian-soviet-states-populated-by-cainites-or-kueijin?p=959319#post959319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Kue-Jin definition of &quot;Asian&quot; then? It's seems incredibly nebulous and arbitrary, which makes me question why it even exists as a distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a kuei-jin creation standpoint, &quot;Asia&quot; seems to be defined in relation to the afterlife. Specifically, those lands and places where the Yama Kings can claim damned souls from. Every kuei-jin is a fugitive from Yomi, after all. So if you can't go to Yomi, you can't come back as a kuei-jin. That includes China, Japan, India, Malaysia, Vietnam, Thailand . . .<br /> <br /> Its a consequence of some of the ideas in Mage and Wraith. Belief shapes the afterlife - the powers that the local wraiths can manifest, the size/strength of the Dark Kingdom, how easily beings &quot;from beyond&quot; can reach into the world of the living . . . Its even a phenomena that impacts visiting wraiths - stay too long, and they can be trapped in an alien mythos.<br /> <br /> (Westerners shouldn't get too cocky, though. There are <i>plenty</i> of bad things waiting to torment you in the Western afterlife, after all)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}